Result

Thus, the program successfully translates a valid logical address into a physical address using base and limit registers and rejects invalid addresses.

2. Paging Memory Management Scheme
Aim

To implement a program that demonstrates the paging memory management scheme using pages, frames, and a page table.

Concept

Paging divides:

Logical memory into fixed-size pages.
Physical memory into fixed-size frames.

A logical address consists of:

Logical Address=(Page Number,Offset)

The page table maps the page number to a frame number.

The physical address is:

Physical Address=Frame Number×Page Size+Offset
Algorithm
Read the page size.
Read the number of pages.
Enter the frame number corresponding to each page.
Read the page number and offset.
Check whether the page number is valid.
Check whether the offset is within the page size.
Obtain the frame number from the page table.
Calculate the physical address.
Display the result.
C Program
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int pageSize, numPages;
    int pageTable[100];
    int pageNumber, offset;
    int frameNumber, physicalAddress;
    int i;

    printf("Enter page size: ");
    scanf("%d", &pageSize);

    printf("Enter number of pages: ");
    scanf("%d", &numPages);

    printf("\nEnter frame number for each page:\n");

    for (i = 0; i < numPages; i++) {
        printf("Page %d -> Frame: ", i);
        scanf("%d", &pageTable[i]);
    }

    printf("\nEnter page number: ");
    scanf("%d", &pageNumber);

    printf("Enter offset: ");
    scanf("%d", &offset);

    if (pageNumber < 0 || pageNumber >= numPages) {
        printf("\nInvalid Page Number!\n");
    }
    else if (offset < 0 || offset >= pageSize) {
        printf("\nInvalid Offset!\n");
    }
    else {
        frameNumber = pageTable[pageNumber];

        physicalAddress = frameNumber * pageSize + offset;

        printf("\nPage Number      : %d\n", pageNumber);
        printf("Offset           : %d\n", offset);
        printf("Frame Number     : %d\n", frameNumber);
        printf("Physical Address : %d\n", physicalAddress);
    }

    return 0;
}
