Result

Thus, the paging memory management scheme was successfully implemented using a page table to translate logical addresses into physical addresses.

3. Simulation of a Page Table
Aim

To develop a program that accepts page table entries and logical addresses and maps logical pages to physical frames.

Concept

A page table maintains the mapping:

Page Number → Frame Number

For example:

Page 0 → Frame 4
Page 1 → Frame 2
Page 2 → Frame 7
Page 3 → Frame 1

If the logical address contains:

Page = 2
Offset = 50

and page 2 is mapped to frame 7:

Physical Address=(7×PageSize)+50
Algorithm
Read the number of pages.
Read the page size.
Enter the frame number for every page.
Display the page table.
Read a logical page number and offset.
Find the corresponding frame number.
Calculate the physical address.
Display the translation.
C Program
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int pageTable[100];
    int numPages, pageSize;
    int pageNumber, offset;
    int frameNumber, physicalAddress;
    int i;

    printf("Enter number of pages: ");
    scanf("%d", &numPages);

    printf("Enter page size: ");
    scanf("%d", &pageSize);

    printf("\nEnter Page Table Entries:\n");

    for (i = 0; i < numPages; i++) {
        printf("Page %d -> Frame: ", i);
        scanf("%d", &pageTable[i]);
    }

    printf("\n--- Page Table ---\n");
    printf("Page\tFrame\n");

    for (i = 0; i < numPages; i++) {
        printf("%d\t%d\n", i, pageTable[i]);
    }

    printf("\nEnter logical page number: ");
    scanf("%d", &pageNumber);

    printf("Enter offset: ");
    scanf("%d", &offset);

    if (pageNumber < 0 || pageNumber >= numPages) {
        printf("\nInvalid page number!\n");
    }
    else if (offset < 0 || offset >= pageSize) {
        printf("\nInvalid offset!\n");
    }
    else {
        frameNumber = pageTable[pageNumber];

        physicalAddress =
            frameNumber * pageSize + offset;

        printf("\n--- Address Translation ---\n");
        printf("Logical Page Number : %d\n", pageNumber);
        printf("Offset              : %d\n", offset);
        printf("Mapped Frame Number : %d\n", frameNumber);
        printf("Physical Address    : %d\n", physicalAddress);
    }

    return 0;
}
